  "summary": "The repair widens the sealed unit registry's table of accepted spellings so that the typographic unit symbols models actually emit — the ohm sign, the middle-dot product separator, and superscript exponent digits — resolve to exactly the same canonical units as their already-accepted ASCII counterparts, and correspondingly amends the frozen answer-form contract so those spellings are admitted as resolvable answer forms rather than passing the form gate and then terminating as undecidable. No physics, tolerance, or comparison semantics change; only which written spellings the registry can name.",
